<div class="page">

<!-- COVER — SANITISED SHAREABLE EDITION -->


<!-- PLATFORM CONTEXT + KEY TERMS -->
<section class="card" id="context">
  <div class="kicker">Platform context and key terms — read first</div>
  <h2>Analytics Platform, source definitions</h2>

  <p>Analytics Platform is the organisation's Data Processing Platform medallion analytical data lake operating a Bronze (raw ingest) → Silver (conform) → Gold (analytical serving) pipeline. All options in this document describe work that lands in, transforms within, or is served from Analytics Platform's medallion layers.</p>

  <div class="platform-box">
    <h4>Analytics Platform medallion layer structure — confirmed current state</h4>
    <div class="platform-layers">
      <div class="platform-layer b">
        <h5>&#129683; Bronze — Raw ingest</h5>
        <p>Immutable managed tables. Schema-versioned. Retained for history replay.<br><br>
        <strong>Currently in Bronze:</strong> Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform buying and merchandising ingest. Product Information Platform product attributes and category hierarchy ingest. Both pipelines complete.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-layer s">
        <h5>&#9889; Silver — Conform</h5>
        <p>Cleansed, canonical, quality-assured managed tables. Platform Data Catalogue lineage.<br><br>
        <strong>Currently in Silver:</strong> Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform buy-side data (fully governed). Product Information Platform product attributes via Product Content API pathway. Product Information Platform category hierarchy via Category API pathway.<br><br>
        <strong>Not in Silver:</strong> Price domain, Inventory, Promotions, Review data, Specialist Product Domain — aggregation-service-derived operational domains only available via Document Database and Relational Database.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-layer g">
        <h5>&#127775; Gold — Analytics</h5>
        <p>DS-optimised outputs with consumer contracts.<br><br>
        <strong>Currently in Gold:</strong> Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform buy-side analytical tables. DS squads consume these.<br><br>
        <strong>Not in Gold:</strong> Product Information Platform product attributes and hierarchy — available in Silver but never promoted to Gold. DS squads cannot consume Product Information Platform data from Analytics Platform Gold today despite it existing in Silver.<br><br>
        <strong>Gap:</strong> No Consumer Analytics Data Product unified product Gold layer exists. This programme creates it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sh">Source and term definitions</div>
  <div class="terms-grid">
    <div class="term-card t-a">
      <div class="term-name">Source A — Analytics Platform-governed product data</div>
      <div class="term-body">Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform buy-side data (Bronze → Silver → Gold, fully governed) and Product Information Platform product attributes and hierarchy (Bronze → Silver, governed but NOT yet promoted to Gold). Source A is richer than previously described — it includes both buy-side structure and Product Information Platform product content in Silver.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-b">
      <div class="term-name">Source B — aggregation-service-derived operational domains not in Analytics Platform</div>
      <div class="term-body">The operational domains aggregated by the Product Aggregation Service that have no Analytics Platform representation: price, inventory/stock, promotions, review data and a specialist product domain. These flow from Product Aggregation Service to Document Database (Consumer Teams A and B) and Relational Database with time-series extension (Consumer Team C) only. Sourcing these into Analytics Platform is the AO-2 ingestion programme.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-gap">
      <div class="term-name">The Product Information Platform Gold promotion gap</div>
      <div class="term-body">Product Information Platform product attributes and hierarchy are in Analytics Platform Silver but have never been promoted to a governed Gold analytical layer. DS squads cannot consume Product Information Platform data from Analytics Platform Gold. They may therefore be consuming Product Information Platform-derived data from Document Database instead, unaware it is available in Analytics Platform Silver. Resolving this is Workstream 1 of AO-1 — no new ingestion required.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-gap">
      <div class="term-name">The DS consumption split (undocumented)</div>
      <div class="term-body">DS squads consume from both Analytics Platform Gold (Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform tables) and their aggregation-service-fed stores (Document Database for Consumer Teams A and B, Relational Database for Consumer Team C). The exact field-level split — which features come from Analytics Platform and which from Product Aggregation Service stores — is not documented. Q1 must surface this as part of the field coverage analysis.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-dso">
      <div class="term-name">Consumer Analytics Data Product and Consumer Analytics Optimised</div>
      <div class="term-body">Consumer Analytics Data Product is the new Consumer Analytics-optimised analytical layer inside Analytics Platform Gold. Consumer Analytics Optimised is the physical Gold-layer managed table within it, assembling governed Source A Silver data (Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform + Product Information Platform) and, later, Source B domain feeds. It does not yet exist — this programme creates it.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-platform">
      <div class="term-name">Analytics Platform to Source Crosswalk</div>
      <div class="term-body">A Silver or Gold-layer managed table mapping Analytics Platform canonical Article ID to source system identifiers across Document Database, Relational Database and Product Aggregation Service. Resolves the leading-zero and identifier inconsistency problem confirmed in the field validation exercise.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-dso">
      <div class="term-name">Compatibility View</div>
      <div class="term-body">A Gold-layer managed view preserving the field shape DS squads currently expect from their Document Database and Relational Database stores. Enables squad migration without immediate model pipeline rewrites. Carries a mandatory exit date — not a permanent contract.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="term-card t-b">
      <div class="term-name">Product Aggregation Service</div>
      <div class="term-body">An aggregation interface combining multiple upstream APIs, including product content, category, stock, price, offers, reviews and a specialist product feed. It feeds a Document Database through event streaming and batch processing for Consumer Teams A and B, and a Relational Database with a time-series extension for Consumer Team C. It also populates a Search Platform. Product Aggregation Service is not authoritative for any single domain.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ROADMAP -->
<section class="card" id="roadmap">
  <div class="kicker">Roadmap overview</div>
  <h2>Four-phase delivery sequence</h2>

  <div class="timeline-strip">
    <div class="tl-phase p1">
      <h4>Phase 1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 0–6 weeks</h4>
      <p>Profile required fields against Analytics Platform Gold, Silver and source systems. Document DS squad consumption split. Answer Q1–Q4. No architecture committed before this completes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-phase p2">
      <h4>Phase 2 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 6–14 weeks</h4>
      <p>AO-1: Promote Product Information Platform and Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform Silver → Consumer Analytics Data Product Gold. Add Crosswalk and Compatibility Views. Source B bootstrap for fields absent from Analytics Platform entirely.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-phase p3">
      <h4>Phase 3 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 3–9 months</h4>
      <p>AO-2: Direct bulk feeds from Pricing, Inventory, Promotions, Reviews into Analytics Platform Bronze → Silver → Gold. Retire Source B bootstrap. Migrate DS consumers to output ports.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-phase p4">
      <h4>Phase 4 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 9–18 months</h4>
      <p>AO-3: Selective CDC into Bronze only where Q4 confirms a sub-daily freshness requirement. Silver batch always retained as reconciliation baseline.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

