  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th style="width:5%">#</th><th style="width:30%">Question</th><th style="width:35%">How to answer it</th><th style="width:15%">Output</th><th style="width:15%">Confidence without it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Q1</strong></td>
          <td>Which of the required DS fields fall into each of three buckets: in Analytics Platform Gold already; in Analytics Platform Silver but not Gold; absent from Analytics Platform entirely? Also: what does each DS squad currently consume from Analytics Platform Gold vs from their Product Aggregation Service store?</td>
          <td>Field-by-field profile against Analytics Platform Gold and Silver schemas. Cross-reference against DS squad model feature catalogues (if documented) to establish the current Analytics Platform vs Product Aggregation Service consumption split. Executable within Analytics Platform by one data engineer — no external dependency.</td>
          <td>Three-bucket field map plus DS consumption split. Defines the exact scope of every subsequent workstream.</td>
          <td><span class="tag d">Low — the delivery path, effort and team dependency differ completely across the three buckets. Without Q1, every estimate in this document is a guess.</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Q2</strong></td>
          <td>For Bucket 3 fields (absent from Analytics Platform entirely), which system is the authoritative source — not the nearest aggregator (Product Aggregation Service)?</td>
          <td>Source authority register workshop with Pricing, Inventory, Promotions and Reviews domain owners. Map each absent field to a named owning system and team.</td>
          <td>Source authority register. Prevents Product Aggregation Service being selected as the default Bronze source for fields that should come from the authoritative operational system directly.</td>
          <td><span class="tag d">Low — without this, Source B bootstrap defaults to Product Aggregation Service for all Bucket 3 fields permanently.</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Q3</strong></td>
          <td>What bulk extract or CDC interface does each authoritative Bucket 3 domain system officially support for Bronze ingestion into Analytics Platform?</td>
          <td>Engagement with Pricing, Inventory, Promotions and Reviews platform teams. Ask: does a bulk export exist? Is there a CDC stream? What are the contractual terms and SLAs for Analytics Platform as a consumer?</td>
          <td>Interface inventory per domain. Determines AO-2 delivery sequencing and which domains need a Product Aggregation Service bridge in the interim.</td>
          <td><span class="tag a">Medium — Bucket 3 domain interfaces for direct Analytics Platform ingestion are unvalidated.</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Q4</strong></td>
          <td>What freshness does each DS use case require per attribute — confirmed with a named business owner?</td>
          <td>DS squad leads confirm per use case in writing. Distinguish: daily batch sufficient; sub-daily required. Named business owner required for any sub-daily claim.</td>
          <td>Freshness register. Gates all AO-3 CDC decisions. Current DS requirements appear batch-oriented — no sub-daily requirement has been documented.</td>
          <td><span class="tag d">Low — AO-3 must not be built without this evidence.</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
