    <div class="ws-card fast">
      <h4>&#9312; Workstream 1 — Silver to Gold promotion</h4>
      <p>Surface Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform Gold tables and promote Product Information Platform Silver data into the new Consumer Analytics Optimised Gold managed table. Add managed-table quality constraints, Platform Data Catalogue lineage, Crosswalk managed table, and a daily history snapshot scheduler. Build Compatibility Views per squad. This is entirely internal Analytics Platform Data Processing Platform work — no external team, no Bronze ingest, no interface negotiation. The governed data already exists in Silver; the work is making it consumable from Gold.</p>
      <div class="ws-meta">No external dependency &nbsp;·&nbsp; Highest delivery confidence &nbsp;·&nbsp; Covers Buckets 1 and 2</div>
    </div>
    <div class="ws-card mid">
      <h4>&#9313; Workstream 2 — Source B bootstrap for Bucket 3</h4>
      <p>For fields Q1 confirms are absent from Analytics Platform entirely (Bucket 3 — Price domain, Inventory, Promotions, Reviews, Specialist Product Domain), establish a new time-boxed Bronze ingest from Product Aggregation Service as a bootstrap. This is a new Bronze landing pipeline — not an existing connection. Bronze → Silver conform jobs add quality controls and lineage. The bootstrap is explicitly scoped to Bucket 3 fields confirmed by Q1, carries mandatory exit conditions, and is retired field by field as AO-2 delivers authoritative domain feeds.</p>
      <div class="ws-meta">New Product Aggregation Service Bronze ingest required &nbsp;·&nbsp; Medium confidence &nbsp;·&nbsp; Covers Bucket 3 only &nbsp;·&nbsp; Mandatory exit conditions</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="exit-box">
    <strong>&#128680; Mandatory exit conditions — agreed in writing before Workstream 2 is activated</strong><br><br>
    <strong>Source B Bronze bootstrap (Workstream 2):</strong> Retires field by field as AO-2 delivers authoritative domain Bronze feeds for those fields and they are validated in Silver. Owner: Data Engineering Manager. Maximum: 6 months per field from activation. Architecture review triggered automatically if not retired by deadline.<br><br>
    <strong>Compatibility Views (Gold):</strong> Retire when each DS squad's model pipelines complete migration to AO-2 output port contracts. Owner: named DS squad lead per squad. Maximum: 3 months from AO-2 delivery date.<br><br>
    <strong>Consumer Analytics Optimised Gold table:</strong> Not retired — promoted to AO-2 assembly output. Must be designed AO-2 compatible from day one.
  </div>

  <h3>Trade-offs</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th style="width:50%">&#10003; Advantages</th><th style="width:50%">&#10007; Limitations / Risks</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="pro">Workstream 1 deliverable within weeks — no external dependency.</span> Product Information Platform Silver and Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform Gold data already exist and are governed in Analytics Platform. The work is creating the Gold managed table, adding quality constraints, and scheduling the daily snapshot. One data engineer with Analytics Platform access.</td><td><span class="con">Bucket 1 and 2 coverage is unknown until Q1 completes.</span> If Q1 reveals Enterprise Resource Platform / Product Lifecycle Platform Gold and Product Information Platform Silver together cover most of the required fields, Workstream 2 scope is small. If they cover few, the Source B bootstrap scope is larger and carries more Product Aggregation Service artefact risk.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pro">Product Information Platform Gold promotion resolves the most impactful gap without new ingestion.</span> DS squads may be unnecessarily pulling Product Information Platform-derived data from Document Database when the governed version is already in Analytics Platform Silver. Workstream 1 makes it directly consumable.</td><td><span class="con">Workstream 2 Source B bootstrap carries Product Aggregation Service aggregation artefacts.</span> Price domain, Inventory, Promotions and Reviews data sourced from Product Aggregation Service carries Product Aggregation Service's field naming and value encoding. Semantic mismatches must be documented before promotion to Silver. <code>is_active</code> and <code>title</code> mismatches are confirmed — others are likely.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pro">The AO-2 durable path is built in parallel.</span> The Source B bootstrap in Workstream 2 is a temporary placeholder that AO-2 domain feeds retire. Consumer Analytics Optimised Gold is designed to swap in authoritative Silver sources as they arrive — no rebuild.</td><td><span class="con">Workstream 2 Source B bootstrap is a NEW Bronze ingest from Product Aggregation Service.</span> This is not an existing connection — it requires a new Bronze landing pipeline to be built and Product Aggregation Service's cooperation. This is different from previous versions which incorrectly described an existing Document Database→Analytics Platform connection.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Rationale</h3>
  <p>AO-1 is the recommended Phase 2 approach. Workstream 1 is the fastest confirmed delivery path in the programme — it requires no external team, no new Bronze ingest, and no interface negotiation. The Product Information Platform Silver-to-Gold promotion alone may cover a substantial portion of the required field set without any Source B work. Q1 is the essential prerequisite: until Bucket 1, Bucket 2 and Bucket 3 are defined, the scope of Workstream 2 and the entire AO-2 programme is unknown.</p>
</section>

